 "summary": "No declaration in Mathlib or TauCeti covers derivative-sign order-convexity, Thom root encodings, or the exact 0/1 sign-count reconstruction, and the PR consumes the existing Rolle, occCount/signCount, and fullInverse/Tarski-query APIs rather than re-deriving them. The Fin-indexed layer is required by the Fintype-indexed counting API and is now derived from the \u2115-indexed layer through the single helper `derivativeSign_tail`, so it is not a parallel API.",
